# SM-T715 (armv7h) rebuild of Arch's libcamera 0.7.2-4 for the Galaxy Tab
# S2's cameras, on omarchy-mobile's software-ISP patch series.
#
# Why: the tablet's cameras have no ISP. The t715-camera kernel driver
# (kernel/patches/t715-parity, kernel/patches/t715-camera-af) captures raw
# Bayer through CSIS and FIMC-LITE straight to memory, which the simple
# pipeline handler with the software ISP turns into pictures: stock
# libcamera ignores the receiver, because the simple handler matches only
# a fixed table of media-device driver names. omarchy-mobile
# (https://github.com/derekross/omarchy-mobile, packages/libcamera, MIT)
# builds the same 0.7.2-4 for a Pixel 7 Pro with a 56-patch series that
# gives the software ISP contrast autofocus with a lens, lens shading,
# denoise, sharpening and defective-pixel correction on the GPU, a better
# AGC/AWB and manual controls: 0001-0056 here are that series, unchanged.
# 0057 adds this tablet's receiver to the table, 0058 its two sensors
# (S5K4H5 rear, S5K6B2 front: black level 64, gain code/32, both measured
# on the tablet), 0059 their tuning files (the rear's Af
# scans the DW9807's useful travel, 400 to 700; no colour matrix, which
# makes the CPU debayer 60% dearer). Package notes:
# docs/image/PACKAGES.md; the cameras: docs/hardware/CAMERA.md.
#
# Base: https://gitlab.archlinux.org/archlinux/packaging/packages/libcamera
# tag 0.7.2-4, which ALARM builds unchanged for armv7h. Changes from
# omarchy-mobile's aarch64 build: pkgrel 4.x (ours sorts above ALARM's
# 0.7.2-4; theirs is 4.22), arch armv7h, no libpisp (the trimmed build
# builds no rpi pipeline that links it), sdl2 resolved through
# sdl2-compat's provide, and the tablet's patches after theirs. The git
# source is pinned by the sha256 of "git archive v0.7.2", as makepkg
# computes it (omarchy-mobile pins the same tree by its sha512).
# Build: tools/build-pkg libcamera (an hour or two under qemu).

# SPDX-License-Identifier: 0BSD
#
# Omarchy Mobile build of libcamera for the Pixel 7 Pro (gs201 CSIS receiver).
#
# Derived from Arch Linux's libcamera PKGBUILD, tag 0.7.2-4
# (https://gitlab.archlinux.org/archlinux/packaging/packages/libcamera, 0BSD),
# which Arch Linux ARM builds unchanged for aarch64. Omarchy Mobile changes:
#  - aarch64 only. Pipelines simple and uvcvideo (USB cameras through
#    USB-C), IPA simple only: none of the other aarch64 pipelines (rkisp1,
#    rpi/*, imx8-isi, mali-c55) can match on this phone, and a smaller
#    native build.
#  - softisp-gpu forced on, so a missing EGL fails the build instead of
#    silently leaving the GPU debayer out. At runtime the GPU path is
#    tried first and falls back to the CPU; LIBCAMERA_SOFTISP_MODE=cpu
#    forces the CPU path.
#  - No documentation (no libcamera-docs split, no Doxygen, Sphinx or
#    TeX Live in the build) and no test suite (test=false, no check()).
#  - werror=false: GCC 16's -Warray-bounds flags libstdc++'s own std::mutex
#    construction in camera_manager.cpp and log.cpp (a false positive in the
#    library headers), which -Werror turned into a failed build.
#  - The 0001-0056 patches, each described in the header of the one before:
#    the gs201 receiver, sensors, contrast autofocus, GPU debayer passes,
#    AGC/AWB, manual controls and tuning. See README.md.
#
# Maintainers of the original: David Runge, Carl Smedstad.

pkgbase=libcamera
